earshot parity fixtures (tools/earshot-parity), third-party credits

The fixtures under fixtures/ are build-time test data for @taalcut/audio. They are not part of the app.

earshot
  Every result under fixtures/ (cli/, intermediates/, kits/) is the output of earshot 0.4.0
  (https://github.com/Leonxlnx/earshot, commit ff41f0788ae56896fd59879ab03858d223c06a53), and the 14 clips in
  fixtures/clips/sfx are renders of its sound bank. Copyright (c) 2026 Leon Lin, MIT licence: see
  third_party/earshot/LICENSE.

Models whose outputs are recorded
  - CLAP, laion/larger_clap_general at revision 16c8cc3159a3c8a31e8ff5ef1f66b0d9ab3667db, by LAION. Apache License
    2.0. The fixtures hold embeddings and scores it computed, not its weights.
  - AST, MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593 at revision f826b80d28226b62986cc218e5cec390b1096902, by Yuan
    Gong, Yu-An Chung and James Glass (MIT CSAIL). BSD 3-Clause License. The fixtures hold logits, probabilities
    and front-end features it computed, not its weights.

AudioSet class names
  fixtures/intermediates/ast.json (`labels`) holds the 527 class names of AudioSet, as the AST model's id2label
  lists them, and fixtures/cli/describe.json and fixtures/cli/timeline.json name some of them in earshot's results.
  The names come from AudioSet's class_labels_indices.csv (https://research.google.com/audioset/), by Google Inc.,
  licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). They are used unchanged, as label names only. The AudioSet data is
  provided as is, without warranties of any kind (CC BY 4.0, section 5). Nothing from the AudioSet ontology file
  (ontology.json, CC BY-SA 4.0) is included: no class descriptions, no hierarchy.
